But then we missed a weekend away together,

264
00:12:28,600 --> 00:12:30,120
and things kind of unraveled...

265
00:12:31,040 --> 00:12:32,160
...because of you.

266
00:12:33,940 --> 00:12:34,660
Happy birthday.

267
00:12:36,740 --> 00:12:37,720
Ross, Rachel promised

268
00:12:37,720 --> 00:12:38,860
it would be over by now.

269
00:12:39,260 --> 00:12:40,600
We seriously have to go

270
00:12:40,600 --> 00:12:41,700
if we want to get to Vermont.

271
00:12:41,780 --> 00:12:42,440
I called them,

272
00:12:42,460 --> 00:12:43,940
the last train leaves in a half-hour.

273
00:12:44,180 --> 00:12:46,120
And I have a massage client soon.

274
00:12:46,320 --> 00:12:48,900
You guys, just, please, a little bit longer.

275
00:12:49,000 --> 00:12:49,560
I promise,

276
00:12:49,640 --> 00:12:51,520
Rachel will be back with the cake any minute.

277
00:12:51,840 --> 00:12:54,540
Monica, remember the frosting, huh?

278
00:12:54,900 --> 00:12:56,840
All right, five more minutes.

279
00:13:00,340 --> 00:13:00,860
Hello?

280
00:13:02,180 --> 00:13:03,220
Oh, no, what happened?

281
00:13:04,680 --> 00:13:06,520
Okay, okay, where are you?

282
00:13:07,060 --> 00:13:08,460
Okay, I'll be right there.

283
00:13:09,520 --> 00:13:10,100
Was that Emma?

284
00:13:10,100 --> 00:13:10,640
Is she up?

285
00:13:13,020 --> 00:13:14,360
Rachel got pulled over for speeding.

286
00:13:14,500 --> 00:13:15,400
She forgot her license.

287
00:13:15,840 --> 00:13:16,940
I have to bring it to her.

288
00:13:17,280 --> 00:13:18,960
If you're leaving, I'm definitely going.

289
00:13:19,640 --> 00:13:22,120
Wait, if anybody gets to go, it's us!

290
00:13:22,320 --> 00:13:23,800
We've been complaining the longest!

291
00:13:25,300 --> 00:13:27,560
No, wait, you guys. No, you can't leave.

292
00:13:27,600 --> 00:13:30,700
Rachel already feels bad that the cake's messed up.

293
00:13:30,800 --> 00:13:31,740
How do you think she'll feel

294
00:13:31,780 --> 00:13:33,460
when she comes back and you're gone?

295
00:13:33,980 --> 00:13:35,820
I don't know. You'll tell us on Monday.

296
00:13:38,220 --> 00:13:40,060
Joey, you're in charge, okay?

297
00:13:40,220 --> 00:13:41,840
You make sure nobody leaves.

298
00:13:41,840 --> 00:13:42,760
Got it!

299
00:13:46,020 --> 00:13:47,000
Hey! Where do you think you're going?

300
00:13:47,360 --> 00:13:48,200
To the bathroom.

301
00:13:49,160 --> 00:13:50,480
Well, the rest of you get comfortable,

302
00:13:50,780 --> 00:13:52,380
because we are gonna be here for a--

303
00:13:53,720 --> 00:13:55,040
Wait, there's a window in there.

304
00:13:55,460 --> 00:13:57,120
No! He's not getting away that easy!

305
00:13:59,540 --> 00:14:00,460
What are you doing?

306
00:14:00,460 --> 00:14:01,860
Get the hell out of here!

307
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:11,220
Well, that one did not have Emma's face on it.

308
00:14:12,480 --> 00:14:13,640
- No, it did not. - No.

309
00:14:15,520 --> 00:14:17,620
Well, we'd better get going. It's late.

310
00:14:18,060 --> 00:14:19,620
Jack can't drive at night anymore.

311
00:14:19,680 --> 00:14:21,400
He has trouble staying in his lane.

312
00:14:21,660 --> 00:14:23,540
Last winter I went up on a church lawn

313
00:14:23,620 --> 00:14:25,380
and drove right through a manger scene.

314
00:14:25,640 --> 00:14:27,340
The papers thought it was a hate crime.

315
00:14:32,200 --> 00:14:34,360
- Anyway, it was lovely seeing you. - Okay.

316
00:14:34,602 --> 00:14:36,900
- Bye. Bye, dear. - Nighty-night.

317
00:14:36,920 --> 00:14:37,820
- Nighty-night. - Bye.

318
00:14:40,060 --> 00:14:41,360
How could you just let them leave?

319
00:14:41,600 --> 00:14:42,080
Hey, hey, hey.

320
00:14:42,080 --> 00:14:43,160
I'm not gonna mess with Jack.

321
00:14:43,160 --> 00:14:44,920
He's a great man. He fought for our country.

322
00:14:46,020 --> 00:14:47,080
No, he didn't.

323
00:14:47,260 --> 00:14:48,520
He pretended to be a Quaker

324
00:14:48,520 --> 00:14:49,480
to get out of Korea.

325
00:14:51,380 --> 00:14:52,800
Well, that's it. He's the last one to go.

326
00:14:52,800 --> 00:14:54,420
I'm locking you guys in.

327
00:14:56,080 --> 00:14:57,460
You do know I can just turn them

328
00:14:57,460 --> 00:14:58,820
the other way around, right?

329
00:15:00,400 --> 00:15:01,780
Oh, I forgot you used to live here.

330
00:15:08,260 --> 00:15:10,020
- Hello? - Joey, it's Estelle.

331
00:15:10,500 --> 00:15:13,580
- Hey. - So how'd your audition go today?

332
00:15:14,020 --> 00:15:14,700
What audition?

333
00:15:14,980 --> 00:15:17,200
The one I told you about last week.

334
00:15:17,440 --> 00:15:19,320
What? You never said anything about an audition.

335
00:15:23,340 --> 00:15:24,280
Let me start over.

336
00:15:25,040 --> 00:15:27,480
I just got a call about an audition.

337
00:15:28,760 --> 00:15:30,460
I think you can still make it.

338
00:15:30,640 --> 00:15:32,580
It's down at the Astor Theater,

339
00:15:32,860 --> 00:15:34,720
and you need to have a monologue prepared.

340
00:15:35,180 --> 00:15:36,980
A monologue? I don't have a--

341
00:15:40,920 --> 00:15:41,880
I got it.

342
00:15:44,260 --> 00:15:46,200
So I'm gonna take off.

343
00:15:46,540 --> 00:15:47,140
What?

344
00:15:47,300 --> 00:15:48,900
No, wait! You don't get to leave.

345
00:15:49,040 --> 00:15:52,160
I've got a massage client waiting outside my door any minute.

346
00:15:52,700 --> 00:15:53,720
And we paid for a room

347
00:15:53,760 --> 00:15:55,500
that we're supposed to be in right now!

348
00:15:55,600 --> 00:15:56,600
Well, okay, now...

349
00:15:57,580 --> 00:15:59,240
...only one of us has to stay with Emma.

350
00:16:00,600 --> 00:16:03,160
Okay, and as the person who realized that, I get to go.

351
00:16:03,360 --> 00:16:05,130
No...

352
00:16:05,600 --> 00:16:08,140
Let's figure out a fair way to decide who's staying.

353
00:16:08,940 --> 00:16:10,380
Oh, I got it.

354
00:16:10,980 --> 00:16:14,000
Okay, everyone pick a number from one to 10, all right?

355
00:16:14,060 --> 00:16:16,180
Whoever gets the highest number gets to go first.

356
00:16:18,940 --> 00:16:19,760
Okay, 10.

357
00:16:19,900 --> 00:16:21,540
Okay, Monica picks 10. I call nine.

358
00:16:21,580 --> 00:16:22,060
Anyone else?

359
00:16:24,060 --> 00:16:25,780
- No, let's just draw straws. - Okay.

360
00:16:26,600 --> 00:16:29,120
Or we could flip a coin and multiply the answer--

361
00:16:29,120 --> 00:16:30,540
- I'm begging you to stop. - Right.

362
00:16:31,980 --> 00:16:33,280
Okay, how about this?

363
00:16:33,360 --> 00:16:34,740
We got wind-up toys for Emma.

364
00:16:35,800 --> 00:16:36,880
We can make them race,

365
00:16:36,960 --> 00:16:39,120
and whoever comes in last stays.

366
00:16:39,240 --> 00:16:40,500
Yeah, let's do that!

367
00:16:41,960 --> 00:16:43,340
That sounds more fun than the thing

368
00:16:43,340 --> 00:16:44,440
we were gonna do in Vermont!

369
00:16:44,780 --> 00:16:46,240
Okay, everybody, pick your toys!

370
00:16:47,220 --> 00:16:48,620
Okay. I want the dolphin!

371
00:16:48,740 --> 00:16:50,460
- That's a bear! - I'm too excited!

372
00:16:52,900 --> 00:16:53,840
Phoebe, you get the bear.

373
00:16:54,660 --> 00:16:55,170
Joey, you get the robot.

374
00:16:55,190 --> 00:16:55,540
Oh, yeah.

375
00:16:55,560 --> 00:16:57,180
And Chandler and I get the dog.

376
00:16:57,620 --> 00:17:02,080
And the race is going to go from here to here.

377
00:17:02,460 --> 00:17:05,360
Now, the one who comes in last stays!

378
00:17:05,660 --> 00:17:06,840
Okay, ladies and gentlemen,

379
00:17:06,880 --> 00:17:07,760
wind your toys.

380
00:17:08,120 --> 00:17:10,020
Okay. On your mark, get set, go!

381
00:17:11,920 --> 00:17:12,540
Go! Go!

382
00:17:12,640 --> 00:17:13,320
Come on, robot!

383
00:17:16,280 --> 00:17:17,780
What are you barking at?

384
00:17:24,280 --> 00:17:26,160
Well, how is that gonna help?

385
00:17:27,180 --> 00:17:28,100
I bought you!

386
00:17:28,160 --> 00:17:30,220
How did I forget that that's all you do?

387
00:17:31,480 --> 00:17:32,420
Way to go, robot!

388
00:17:33,860 --> 00:17:35,020
Good job, Alan.

389
00:17:36,420 --> 00:17:38,080
Hey, good race, you guys.

390
00:17:38,080 --> 00:17:38,920
Yeah, see you later.

391
00:17:39,060 --> 00:17:40,840
No. No, no. Wait.

392
00:17:41,280 --> 00:17:42,680
We didn't lose.

393
00:17:43,320 --> 00:17:44,880
The rules clearly stated that

394
00:17:44,880 --> 00:17:47,360
the last one to cross the finish line was the loser.

395
00:17:47,840 --> 00:17:49,380
Well, our dog never crossed

396
00:17:49,380 --> 00:17:50,900
the finish line. So technically--

397
00:17:50,940 --> 00:17:51,560
They left.

398
00:17:58,720 --> 00:18:00,180
There isn't time to go to the bakery.

399
00:18:00,380 --> 00:18:01,520
We're gonna come home.

400
00:18:02,560 --> 00:18:03,440
Everybody left?

401
00:18:05,560 --> 00:18:06,460
All right. Well, just tell Emma

402
00:18:06,480 --> 00:18:08,920
that we'll be there as soon as we can. Bye.

403
00:18:11,560 --> 00:18:12,920
- Rachel! - Oh, God, sorry!

404
00:18:13,320 --> 00:18:14,760
I can't believe they gave you a ticket.

405
00:18:14,760 --> 00:18:15,760
You're such a good driver.

406
00:18:18,860 --> 00:18:20,980
- Emma's awake. - Yeah?

407
00:18:22,270 --> 00:18:23,480
I can't believe this.

408
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:25,560
This is her first birthday,

409
00:18:25,560 --> 00:18:27,380
she's awake, we're not even there.

410
00:18:27,800 --> 00:18:28,540
Everybody left.

411
00:18:28,600 --> 00:18:30,540
We still have this stupid obscene cake.

412
00:18:31,320 --> 00:18:32,700
Hey, maybe I can fix that.

413
00:18:32,730 --> 00:18:34,980
You know, try to turn it into something else.

414
00:18:35,140 --> 00:18:36,980
Oh, don't even bother.

415
00:18:37,700 --> 00:18:39,400
We've already ruined her first birthday.

416
00:18:40,360 --> 00:18:40,720
And do you know

417
00:18:40,740 --> 00:18:42,760
how important these early experiences are,

418
00:18:43,100 --> 00:18:43,920
Ross? Very!

419
00:18:44,300 --> 00:18:47,200
According to the back cover of that book that you gave me.

420
00:18:49,000 --> 00:18:50,640
Rach, she's not gonna remember this.

421
00:18:52,980 --> 00:18:53,540
I guess.

422
00:18:55,520 --> 00:18:57,800
Oh, I just had such an idea

423
00:18:57,800 --> 00:18:59,980
of what this day would be like, you know?

424
00:19:01,320 --> 00:19:02,380
Emma laughing...

425
00:19:02,380 --> 00:19:05,420
...and everybody gathered around her cake,

426
00:19:05,420 --> 00:19:07,100
singing "Happy Birthday."

427
00:19:07,600 --> 00:19:08,640
And then we would all--

428
00:19:08,920 --> 00:19:09,660
Hey, get out of the road,

429
00:19:09,660 --> 00:19:11,200
you stupid student driver!

430
00:19:14,080 --> 00:19:15,260
They have to learn.

431
00:19:18,340 --> 00:19:19,640
- Hey. - What?

432
00:19:19,740 --> 00:19:20,880
This is not bad.

433
00:19:22,140 --> 00:19:25,540
Oh, my God. Look, you made it into a bunny.

434
00:19:25,620 --> 00:19:26,680
How did you do that?

435
00:19:27,120 --> 00:19:30,000
Well, I just made these two things cheeks.

436
00:19:32,220 --> 00:19:34,580
And then I split this to make ears.

437
00:19:35,980 --> 00:19:38,280
Well, I am very impressed.

438
00:19:38,680 --> 00:19:40,440
Some can sing, some can dance.

439
00:19:40,720 --> 00:19:42,460
I, apparently, can turn phallic cakes

440
00:19:42,460 --> 00:19:43,640
into woodland creatures.

441
00:19:46,780 --> 00:19:49,060
Now, another way to organize your stuffed animals

442
00:19:49,060 --> 00:19:50,600
is by size.

443
00:19:50,700 --> 00:19:52,440
I'm sorry, is this a game

444
00:19:52,440 --> 00:19:53,760
for Emma or for Monica?

445
00:19:55,600 --> 00:19:56,020
Game?

446
00:19:57,480 --> 00:20:00,380
Emma, do you even know it's your birthday today?

447
00:20:00,600 --> 00:20:01,440
You're 1.

448
00:20:02,140 --> 00:20:04,520
One year old. That's little.

449
00:20:07,660 --> 00:20:08,860
That's my girl.

450
00:20:10,380 --> 00:20:12,180
That's how old you are.

451
00:20:12,880 --> 00:20:13,880
Did I teach her that?

452
00:20:14,080 --> 00:20:15,920
Did I just impart wisdom?

453
00:20:19,180 --> 00:20:20,360
I want one.

454
00:20:21,760 --> 00:20:22,600
Me too.

455
00:20:28,660 --> 00:20:29,720
There's no one around.

456
00:20:29,800 --> 00:20:30,860
Why don't we just take this one?

457
00:20:32,740 --> 00:20:34,680
- And head to Canada. - I was kidding.

458
00:20:34,800 --> 00:20:36,100
I wasn't. Let's get going.

459
00:20:38,480 --> 00:20:40,300
Hey, are Ross and Rachel back?

460
00:20:40,380 --> 00:20:41,140
No, not yet.

461
00:20:41,380 --> 00:20:43,620
Oh, good, I didn't miss the party.

462
00:20:43,680 --> 00:20:44,880
What about your massage client?

463
00:20:45,200 --> 00:20:47,180
I just felt so bad missing this.

464
00:20:47,180 --> 00:20:49,140
So I just slipped him a little something, you know.

465
00:20:50,590 --> 00:20:52,340
As long as I'm back in five or six hours,

466
00:20:52,400 --> 00:20:53,440
it'll be all right.

467
00:20:55,680 --> 00:20:56,120
Okay.

468
00:20:57,240 --> 00:20:58,380
If Ross and Rachel ask,

469
00:20:58,420 --> 00:21:00,440
I've been here the whole time. The whole time.

470
00:21:02,360 --> 00:21:03,960
I've been here the whole time.

471
00:21:05,860 --> 00:21:07,360
Joey, we just saw you come in.

472
00:21:07,400 --> 00:21:09,260
You ran past us on the stairs.

473
00:21:10,760 --> 00:21:12,180
I don't care that you left.

474
00:21:12,420 --> 00:21:14,000
I'm just glad that you're here.

475
00:21:14,140 --> 00:21:14,900
Thanks, you guys.

476
00:21:15,240 --> 00:21:16,320
Hey, guys, come on.

477
00:21:16,480 --> 00:21:17,660
You gotta see what Emma just did.

478
00:21:18,200 --> 00:21:20,380
- What? - Emma, how old are you?

479
00:21:20,460 --> 00:21:22,020
How old are you today?

480
00:21:26,320 --> 00:21:28,920
Emma, that's right. You're that many.

481
00:21:29,300 --> 00:21:31,680
Oh, my God, our daughter's a genius.

482
00:21:33,680 --> 00:21:35,120
- This means-- - No! No science camp!

483
00:21:35,548 --> 00:21:39,878
Damn it! I'll put a candle on the cake.

484
00:21:40,420 --> 00:21:43,700
Oh, and, Emma, look at your stuffed animals

485
00:21:43,920 --> 00:21:45,220
lined up so neatly.

486
00:21:46,567 --> 00:21:47,637
Thanks.

487
00:21:48,860 --> 00:21:50,880
Okay, here we go.

488
00:21:52,520 --> 00:21:54,680
Emma's first birthday cake.

489
00:21:56,980 --> 00:21:58,560
Go ahead, Emma, blow out the candle.

490
00:21:59,240 --> 00:22:00,360
Come on, Emma. You can do it.

491
00:22:01,600 --> 00:22:02,740
What's wrong? Are you okay?

492
00:22:02,980 --> 00:22:03,980
Oh, yeah, nothing.

493
00:22:04,900 --> 00:22:06,180
These are happy tears.

494
00:22:07,840 --> 00:22:09,120
This is just what I wanted.

495
00:22:11,560 --> 00:22:13,160
Hey, you made it into a bunny.

496
00:22:15,360 --> 00:22:16,940
What is wrong with me?

497
00:22:16,940 --> 00:22:18,580
It looked more delicious when it was a penis.

498
00:22:25,824 --> 00:22:27,762
- Okay, you ready? - Yeah.

499
00:22:27,782 --> 00:22:30,642
- And record. - Okay.

500
00:22:31,080 --> 00:22:32,060
Hi, Emma.

501
00:22:32,900 --> 00:22:35,260
Well, your first birthday is over, and--

502
00:22:35,965 --> 00:22:37,445
Go! Go! Come on!

503
00:22:37,691 --> 00:22:39,511
Go! Go! Come on!

504
00:22:41,840 --> 00:22:44,680
Go! Go, Alan! Run, you hairy bastard!

